WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:00.789 align:start position:0%
 
[Applause]  qatar is getting used to safely hosting  major sporting events during the  pandemic at the end of last year the  country was home to teams from all over  asia  for the final stages of the champions  league  and this club world cup is another big  step for qatar in the build-up to the  main event  next year's world cup this is the second  edition of the fifa club world cup that  we host  however today we're hosting it in  completely different circumstances  we're hosting it during the global  pandemic  of the coronavirus which is obviously  very difficult  but it is also important for us to make  sure we play our part for the safe  return  of football three continental title  winners are already in qatar  all players and staff were tested for  coronavirus before their journey began  and on arrival in doha the teams then  enter a biosecure environment  which includes their hotel training  ground and stadiums  qatar's league champions aldu hale play  al-ashley of  egypt on thursday the winners of that  game get to take on bayern munich  in the semi-finals of course we cannot  travel like before we cannot  walk like before we need to take care  about um  ourselves to take the social distances  so it's not it's not easy but um anyway  we cannot complain  we are lucky to um to play with uh maybe  10 15 20 000 people  is not the case in europe so we are  lucky  stadiums will be at 30 capacity with  three categories of fans allowed to  attend  those that have had the kovid 19 vaccine  those that test negative just ahead of  the match  all those that have had and recovered  from the virus in the last four months  a lot of evidence internationally and  even locally  that those who have contracted the  disease  are immune from the secondary infection  until now we know definitely for six  months and  in some evidences it lasts up to nine  months even  so we've taken more uh restrictive  measures and we said only four months  the hope is that next year's world cup  will be in a post-pandemic environment  but qatar says it's ready for any  eventuality  andy richardson al jazeera doha

